  "subject": "a power cut on an October night and peeling a pomelo together by candlelight on the balcony",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien bossa nova in the Joao Gilberto school, felt in two. Nylon-string guitar playing a batida thumb-and-chord pattern; upright bass in a two-feel; brushes playing a rim-click bossa pattern; a flute obbligato between vocal phrases; Rhodes electric piano comping only on the bridge. Intimate, dry and close, narrow stereo, guitar and voice forward. Breathy, soft female voice, near-spoken, minimal vibrato, phrasing just behind the beat. 124 BPM, D major. Quietly, happily in love in the dark. No strings, no violins, no güiro, no cha-cha percussion, no pop drum kit, no autotune.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n九點半 規條巷仔暗去\n冷氣停 電視嘛恬去\n你摸烏 揣著一枝蠟條\n插佇米酒矸仔頂\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n陽台的風 對河邊吹來\n你講 規氣來剝柚仔\n\n[Chorus]\n停電 嘛無要緊\n一粒柚仔 兩个人慢慢仔剝\n你一齒 我一齒\n酸酸甜甜 免開燈\n\n[Verse]\n你共柚仔皮 剝甲完完整整\n做一頂帽仔 共我戴佇頭殼頂\n你講足媠 我講足戇\n厝邊的狗 嘛吠兩聲\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n蠟條火 輕輕仔咧搖\n你的影 佇壁頂搖來搖去\n\n[Chorus]\n停電 嘛無要緊\n一粒柚仔 兩个人慢慢仔剝\n你一齒 我一齒\n柚仔子 吐佇你的手底\n\n[Bridge]\n十一點 蠟條賰一寸\n你講 欲閣揣一枝\n屜仔 翻甲亂操操\n干焦揣著 生日的蠟條\n\n[Chorus]\n停電 嘛無要緊\n一粒柚仔 兩个人慢慢仔剝\n你一齒 我一齒\n生日蠟條 點三枝\n\n[Outro]\n柚仔皮帽仔\n猶戴佇我頭殼頂",
